-- title:
--   Level automorphisms at Γ(q)∩Γ₀(M') preserve the Gauss prime
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$.
--
--   *Base data.* $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and the hypothesis `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subset L(\!(q)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$), and `hK` identifies it as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise image (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$) of the field of $q$-expansions attached to the congruence subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ and subgroup $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   *Coefficient ring.* $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), $\xi$ lies in the image of $A \to L$ (`hξA`), and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Furthermore $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   *The Hauptmodul and the chart algebra.* The element $j \in K$, assumed nonzero, has Laurent series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$ with coefficients pushed into $L$. Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ (the $j$-finite chart algebra), `jChartFin A K j` is $j$ viewed inside it, `XFin A K j` is its spectrum, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the scheme obtained by glueing the spectra of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras along the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the canonical morphism `ιFin` from `XFin`.
--
--   *The supersingular maximal ideal.* $y$ is a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing the image of $\varpi$, and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   *The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`.* This hypothesis postulates a Drinfeld local chart, with a list of riders, at every relevant point: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under $A \to \Gamma(\text{model})$ and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ and whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition `hss'` as above, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and
--   $$f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   (the subtracted series being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and an isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion $\mathrm{CMP}$ of the stalk $\mathrm{STK}$ at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to seven clauses. Writing $\mathrm{toC} : \mathrm{STK} \to \mathrm{CMP}$ for the completion map, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical map from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\mathrm{STK}$ (the germ at $z$ on the image of `ιFin`, precomposed with the inverses of the relevant affine identifications), the clauses are: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), the automorphism $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself; (iii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ and such $\tau$, the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, such $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ is compatible, via $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, with the restriction of $\tau$; $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element of the form $C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathrm{STK}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct whenever $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing an element $C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a$ in the chart algebra, $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ in $L$; (vii) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $q\ell$, lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of the two lying in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a, b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} (\text{coefficient of } X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i} \text{ in } h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\,)))$ of that difference equals the class of $h$.
--
--   *The chosen point and witness.* A point $z$ of the two-chart integral model is fixed together with $\varpi_z$, its defining equation `hϖz` and the hypothesis `hz` that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk; a point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` above $z$ with the supersingularity condition `hss'` and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`); and one Drinfeld chart $(W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1)$ of the shape described above ($W_1$ a complete discrete valuation domain, $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $u_1, v_1$ units, $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and $e_1$ an isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$), for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the seven clauses (i)–(vii) above verbatim, with $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ in place of $W, \sigma, f, u, v, e$.
--
--   *The automorphism.* Finally $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lies in $\Gamma(q)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$, and $\nu$ is an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K ν`: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on the group [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) having integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ with the series of $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those expansions, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of the Laurent series of $\nu(x)$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\gamma^{-1})$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\gamma^{-1})$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}(m)(\delta)$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/m \\ m\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A K j`, the following two conditions are equivalent: for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ there exists $m \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ whose image in $L$ is the $n$-th coefficient of the Laurent series of $a$; and for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ there exists $m \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ whose image in $L$ is the $n$-th coefficient of the Laurent series of $\nu(a)$.
--
--   The set of elements of the $j$-finite chart algebra all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ is the Gauss prime, the generic point of the Igusa component through the cusp $\infty$; the theorem states that this condition is invariant under the automorphism of $K/L$ attached to any $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, so that the Gauss prime is stable under these level automorphisms. It feeds the comparison of the Gauss prime with the Igusa valuation in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_mem_iff_map_mem_igusaValuation_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_mem_iff_map_mem_igusaValuation_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness), within the analysis of the integral model of the modular curve at the supersingular points in characteristic $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness.lean

